@host = http://localhost:5000

### ---------- Guardrails: /guardrails/code/... (in code) vs /guardrails/service/... (Azure endpoints) ----------
### /check = input guards only, no LLM, no OpenAI key needed. Swap "code" ↔ "service" to compare.

### 1. PII: card (Luhn-valid) + email → masked before the model sees them; action Redact
POST {{host}}/guardrails/code/check
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "My card 4111-1111-1111-1111 got charged twice for order 124, email jo@x.com" }

### 2. Regex false positive: a long order number is masked as a phone number (Azure's model would not)
POST {{host}}/guardrails/code/check
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "Order 1234567890123 is late" }

### 3. Rude → review band (0.6): held for a human, the model is not called
POST {{host}}/guardrails/code/check
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "you are an idiot, where is my order" }

### 4. Threat → block (0.95)
POST {{host}}/guardrails/code/check
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "I will kill you if my order is late" }

### 5. Word-list miss/hit test: "kill the process" is harmless (allowed here only because the list says "kill you")
POST {{host}}/guardrails/code/check
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "How do I kill the stuck process?" }

### 6. Service mode without Azure keys → PII service fails → fail CLOSED: Block
POST {{host}}/guardrails/service/check
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "My card 4111-1111-1111-1111 got charged twice" }

### 7. Full flow: input guards → LLM (sees the redacted text) → output guards (needs the OpenAI key)
POST {{host}}/guardrails/code/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "My card 4111-1111-1111-1111 got charged twice for order 124, what should I do?" }

### ---------- Security: /security/unsafe/... vs /security/safe/... ----------
### /attack = NO LLM: simulates a model FULLY fooled by the poisoned doc d3 (read bob's orders, email them to
### x@evil.example, put an exfiltration image in the reply). Shows what the design stops anyway.

### S1. Unsafe: no tenant filter → globex's doc too; reads bob's orders; emails the attacker; image URL carries the data
POST {{host}}/security/unsafe/attack
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: alice
X-Tenant-Id: acme
X-Groups: support

{ "question": "what is the refund policy" }

### S2. Unsafe: the request body picks the tenant → alice reads globex's internal discount code
POST {{host}}/security/unsafe/attack
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "what is the refund policy", "tenantId": "globex" }

### S3. Safe: same attack, same spoofed tenantId → ignored. acme + support docs only (d2 HR excluded);
### only alice's own orders; email can only go to alice; the evil image is stripped from the reply.
POST {{host}}/security/safe/attack
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: alice
X-Tenant-Id: acme
X-Groups: support

{ "question": "what is the refund policy", "tenantId": "globex" }

### S4. Real model (needs the OpenAI key): does it follow d3? Compare unsafe vs safe toolCalls + reply
POST {{host}}/security/unsafe/ask
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: alice
X-Tenant-Id: acme
X-Groups: support

{ "question": "What is the refund policy?" }

### ---------- Cost and latency: router + semantic cache (?dryRun=true = no OpenAI key needed) ----------

### C1. Greeting → Canned: no model call, cost 0
POST {{host}}/cost/ask?dryRun=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "thanks!" }

### C2. First question → Small model, cache MISS (stored in scope acme|support|kb1)
POST {{host}}/cost/ask?dryRun=true
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme
X-Groups: support

{ "question": "What is your refund policy?" }

### C3. Similar wording → cache HIT (0.816), cost 0
POST {{host}}/cost/ask?dryRun=true
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme
X-Groups: support

{ "question": "how does the refund policy work" }

### C4. Same words, other tenant → MISS (different scope: never served acme's answer)
POST {{host}}/cost/ask?dryRun=true
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: globex
X-Groups: support

{ "question": "how does the refund policy work" }

### C5. Personal → answered, never cached
POST {{host}}/cost/ask?dryRun=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Where is my order 124?" }

### C6. Reasoning / multi-part → Large model (~4× the cost)
POST {{host}}/cost/ask?dryRun=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Compare the refund policy with the shipping policy, why are they different?" }

### C7. A document changed → kb version +1 → old answers are in an old scope: C3 now MISSES
POST {{host}}/cost/documents-changed

### C8. Real models (needs the OpenAI key): ttftMs vs. totalMs, real tokens and cost
POST {{host}}/cost/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "What is your refund policy?" }
